<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ashot Msaker</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 826</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a> · Also known as Ashot IV Bagratuni</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ashot Msaker, the Carnivore, was a Bagratid prince who became presiding prince of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armenia">Armenia</a> under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abbasid-caliphate">Abbasid Caliphate</a> in the early 9th century. He built up the family's lands, which were divided among his sons; one son, Bagrat, received Taron, founding its line of princes. His descendant Ashot I became king of Armenia.</p></div>
